the highly anticipated spider-man no way  home a sequel to 2017's spider-man  homecoming and 2019 spider-man far from  home is finally out in theaters  following a whole lot of rumors about  which characters from previous  spider-man franchises would appear major  spoilers for spider-man no way home  ahead in no way home peter parker is  dealing with the aftermath of his  identity as spider-man being revealed  overwhelmed by the attention and the  consequences he asked dr strange to use  magic to make his identity a secret once  again in the midst of doing so the  multiverse is opened and peter is  suddenly faced with a slew of villains  from other realities who have fought  alternate versions of spider-man those  spider-men toby maguire and andrew  garfield reprising their roles from sam  raimi's films and mark webb's films  respectively show up and help tom  holland's peter save the day as is  typical with any marvel movie no way  home is chock full of easter eggs for  dedicated fans to find and enjoy but  there's one line that even the most  dedicated fans may have missed in terms  of its deeper meaning and it has to do  with some behind the scenes drama in the  film while all three spider-men are  waiting for the villains to arrive to  face off against them toby maguire's  spider-man complains of his back  problems saying that all of his  web-slinging must have exacerbated the  issue andrew garfield's spider-man then  helps him crack his back in a charming  and humorous bit before the action  commences but this bit actually has a  deeper meaning and references some  real-life back problems in maguire's  that played a part in his negotiations  for 2004's spider-man 2. as reported by  variety in 2003 mcguire signed on for  spider-man 2 in a 17 million deal but  not before negotiations became a bit  tense during negotiations columbia  pictures allegedly felt that mcguire's  known back problems quote were now being  used as a threat during negotiations if  the actor's list of demands wasn't met  the studio even considered recasting  mcguire's role by replacing him with  jake gyllenhaal who of course later went  on to star opposite holland and far from  home as mysterio luckily maguire's team  stepped in promising good behavior for  maguire as long as he received checkups  to assure his back was in good condition  the situation definitely sounds tense  which makes a reference in no way home  all the more fun now that all the drama  from the early 2000s is good for a laugh  toby maguire's back problems have become  infamous on hollywood circles so much so  that no way home didn't even contain the  first reference to the situation back in  sam raimi's spider-man 2 maguire's peter  parker is trying to get back into the  groove of this whole superhero thing he  tries to leap between buildings yelling  i'm back only to fall from a  considerable height  my back  open my back  as it turns out sam raimi was nervous  about including the line in the flick  because he didn't want to upset maguire  and told the bbc about a conversation he  had about the situation with his brother  producer ivan ramy he told the bbc  at first i thought that was really funny  and then i said you know ivan although i  think it's funny because we've had this  problem with toby maybe we better not do  it because i mean he has had a back  problem and then ivan says oh screw it  we'll just do it anyways for those who  know about the problem with toby's back  it'll be an inside joke and for those  who don't it should be funny just for  what it is while it wouldn't have made  or broke the film whether the line was  in it or not it would have been a fun  bit for people who kept up with all the  behind the scenes drama as luck would  have it maguire was game raymie told the  bbc i told toby i thought it would be  funny and he said you know what that  will be funny it's okay if they laugh at  me let them laugh at me i thought that  was very brave of him check out one 